    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classBase" kindref="compound">Base</ref> entity for clinic-owned clinical records (patients, visits, reports, ...). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Extends <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> with a fixed organisation name (&quot;clinics&quot;) and a family of static permission-query builders. Concrete service entities derive from <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref> and expose those builders to <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref>, which executes the returned query to decide whether a requester may create/read/update/delete a record. The builders select the owner, admin and staff columns of the owning clinic (joined to the record table where needed). <simplesect kind="note"><para>Unlike the CRUD builders in <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, these queries interpolate the id and table names into the SQL text via fmt::format and take no pqxx::params; they are called with internal, trusted values and the resulting text is also used as a cache key by <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
